<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>Topic 03 - CSS Syntax</title>
    <style>
        body {
            background-color: #1e1e1e;
            color: #d4d4d4;
            font-family: sans-serif;
        }

        /* My heading style */
        h1 {
            color: #4ec9b0;
            font-size: 2rem;
            font-weight: bold;
            text-align: center;
        }

        /* Paragraph formatting */
        p {
            line-height: 1.7;
            max-width: 65ch;
            margin: 0 auto;
        }

        /* Note to self: do not forget the semicolon ; */
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Learning Web Programming at Gachon</h1>
    <p>My name is Thuan. Today I am learning basic CSS syntax. A rule always has a selector, a property, and a value separated by a colon.</p>
</body>
</html>